    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-uttara-kanda-0011",
      "sequence": 994,
      "meaning": "Ayodhya is made exceptionally beautiful while the gods shower flowers. Rama calls his servants and tells them first to bathe his companions; Sugriva and the others are bathed at once. The treasury of compassion then calls Bharata and with his own hands untangles his matted locks. The devotee-loving Lord has all three brothers bathed—a tenderness that even hundreds of millions of Sheshas could not adequately praise. Rama then loosens his own matted hair, asks the guru's permission, bathes and puts on ornaments so beautiful that even the bodiless god of love would be ashamed.",
