    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-uttara-kanda-0012",
      "sequence": 995,
      "meaning": "At the sight of Rama the sage's heart fills with love, and he immediately has a divine throne brought, radiant beyond description like the sun. Rama bows his head to the Brahmins and sits beside Janaka's daughter, delighting the assembly of sages. The Brahmins chant Vedic mantras while gods and sages in the sky cry victory. Vasishtha applies the first coronation mark and directs the other Brahmins to follow. The mothers rejoice to see their son and perform arati repeatedly. Gifts of every kind are given to the Brahmins, making every petitioner need ask no more. Seeing the Lord of the three worlds enthroned, the gods sound their celestial drums.",
