    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-uttara-kanda-0014",
      "sequence": 997,
      "meaning": "Shiva praises Rama, beloved of Lakshmi and remover of becoming's affliction, and asks the Lord of Ayodhya, gods and Lakshmi to protect those who seek refuge. Rama destroyed ten-headed Ravana and his twenty arms and burned the moth-like demon hosts in the fierce fire of his arrows, relieving Earth's pain. Bearing bow, arrow and fine quiver, he adorns the world; the army of his radiance is a sun against the massed night of pride, delusion and possessiveness. The hunter Desire has felled deer-like people with arrows of corrupt pleasure lodged in their hearts; Shiva asks Hari to kill that hunter and protect the helpless wretches lost in the forest of sense objects. People suffer disease and separation as the fruit of disregarding Rama's feet, and those without love for them fall into the unfathomable ocean of becoming. The saints who rely upon his story are free of attachment, greed, pride and intoxication; they treat honour and dishonour, prosperity and adversity alike and joyfully serve him with pure hearts. Shiva worships Raghubira, bee of the sages' mind-lotuses, chants and bows to Hari's name as the great medicine for worldly illness and enemy of pride, and asks the supreme abode of virtue, character and compassion to look upon the lowly and destroy the mass of duality.",
