    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-uttara-kanda-0015",
      "sequence": 998,
      "meaning": "Shiva tells Garuda that this holy account destroys the threefold affliction and fear of worldly existence. Those who hear of Rama's auspicious consecration gain detachment and discernment; those who hear or sing it with desires receive happiness and prosperity in many forms, enjoy happiness rare even to gods and at death go to Raghupati's city. Liberated people, renunciants and householders alike gain devotion, the highest end and renewed abundance. Shiva says he has related Rama's story according to his understanding: it removes fear and pain, strengthens detachment, discernment and devotion, and is a beautiful boat across the river of delusion. Auspiciousness is ever new in Ayodhya, every community remains joyful and love for Rama's lotus feet continually renews. Petitioners receive garments of many kinds and Brahmins receive gifts in many forms.",
