      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-uttara-kanda-0016",
      "sequence": 999,
      "meaning": "Rama's companions forget their homes so completely that they do not recall them even in dreams, just as malice toward others never enters a saint's mind. Raghupati summons them all; they come, bow respectfully and sit close to him in deep love. The giver of happiness to devotees speaks gently: they have rendered extraordinary service, beyond what he can praise to their faces, abandoning home and comfort for his sake. Younger brother, kingdom, wealth, Vaidehi, body, home, family and loved ones are all dear to him, he says, but not equal to them. This is no false statement: every master loves a servant, and Rama's love for his own servants is greater still.",
