      "meaning": "Hearing the Lord, all become so absorbed that they forget who and where they are and even lose awareness of their bodies. They stand before him with folded hands and fixed gaze, too overcome with love to speak. Seeing their supreme devotion, Rama instructs them in knowledge in many ways, yet face to face with him they can only look repeatedly at his lotus feet. The Lord has garments and ornaments of many beautiful colours brought. He first dresses Sugriva, with Bharata arranging the garments by hand; prompted by Rama, Lakshmana dresses Vibhishana, who is dear to Raghupati. Angada alone remains seated and unmoving. Seeing his love, Rama does not tell him to depart.",
