      "meaning": "Angada addresses the all-knowing ocean of compassion and joy, merciful friend of the lowly and distressed. At the time of death, he says, Bali placed him in Rama's care; remembering his renown as refuge of the refuge-less and benefactor of devotees, Rama must not abandon him. Rama is his lord, guru, father and mother—where could he go after leaving those lotus feet? He asks the king to consider what purpose home could hold without the Lord. A child without knowledge, understanding or strength, he begs to remain under protection and perform even the lowest household service; by gazing at Rama's lotus feet he will cross worldly existence. With this plea he falls at Rama's feet and asks not to be told to go home.",
