      "meaning": "Mindful of what his devotees had done, Rama goes with Bharata, Shatrughna and Lakshmana to see them off. Angada's heart brims with love; he repeatedly turns to look toward Rama, bows full-length again and again, and inwardly longs for Rama to tell him to stay. Remembering the Lord's looks, words, gait, smiles and embraces, he grieves. Seeing Rama's intention, he offers many humble words, then leaves with the lotus feet held in his heart. Rama and his brothers respectfully escort all the monkeys. Hanuman then clasps Sugriva's feet and requests permission to serve Raghupati for ten days before returning to see him. Sugriva calls the Wind's son a mass of merit and gladly sends him to serve the abode of compassion. As the monkeys depart swiftly, Angada calls Hanuman aside.",
