      "sequence": 1003,
      "meaning": "The compassionate Lord summons Nishada-raja once more and gives him ornaments and garments as gracious gifts. Rama tells his friend to return home remembering him, to follow dharma in mind, action and speech, and to come and go freely in Ayodhya, for he is as dear as Bharata and a brother. Overcome with joy, Nishada falls at his feet with tear-filled eyes, carries the lotus feet in his heart, returns home and tells his family of the Lord's nature. Seeing Raghupati's conduct, Ayodhya's people repeatedly call the treasury of happiness blessed. Rama takes the throne; the three worlds rejoice and every sorrow departs. No one bears enmity toward another, for Rama's majesty removes social hostility and inequality.",
